---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
import { TumaBoda } from "../components/TumaBoda";
---
<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy" heading="Privacy Policy" path="/privacy"
  lede={`What ${site.name} collects when you order, why, who sees it, and your rights under Kenya's Data Protection Act, 2019.`}>
  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>{site.name}, {site.address}, is the data controller for the personal data described here. You can reach us about it on the details at the end of this page.</p>

  <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
  <p>Only what we need to take and deliver an order:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Contact details:</b> your name, your phone number (which is also your M-Pesa number) and, if you choose to give it, an email address for the receipt.</li>
    <li><b>Delivery details:</b> your area, street and building, and any notes for the <TumaBoda /> rider.</li>
    <li><b>Your order:</b> what you bought, the price, how you paid and when.</li>
    <li><b>Messages:</b> anything you send us on WhatsApp or tell us by phone.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We ask you to confirm that you are 18 or over. <TumaBoda /> riders look at your ID at the door; neither they nor we photograph, copy or keep it. Card payments are made on Paystack's secure page, so we never see or store your card number, and we never see your M-Pesa PIN.</p>

  <h2>3. How it reaches us</h2>
  <p>When you check out on this site, your order comes to us in one of two ways. Either your phone opens WhatsApp with the order written out, and you choose whether to send it; WhatsApp is run by Meta, under its own privacy policy. Or, where online checkout is available, the order is sent straight to our order system.</p>

  <h2>4. Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>To fulfil your order</b> — preparing it, delivering it or getting it ready to collect, taking payment, and contacting you about it. This is necessary to perform our contract with you.</li>
    <li><b>To meet the law</b> — checking that alcohol is only sold to adults, and keeping sales records for tax.</li>
    <li><b>To run the business safely</b> — preventing fraud and handling complaints and refunds, which is in our legitimate interests.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not send marketing messages unless you ask us to, and you can stop them at any time by replying STOP or telling us.</p>

  <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><TumaBoda link />, our delivery partner, which rides every order in Nairobi and gets your name, phone number and delivery address for that order only.</li>
    <li>Safaricom, when you pay by M-Pesa, and Paystack, when you pay by card.</li>
    <li>The companies that host this website and our order system, who process data only on our instructions.</li>
    <li>Authorities, where the law requires us to.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We never sell your personal data.</p>

  <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep order and payment records for five years, as Kenyan tax law requires. Delivery notes and messages are kept only as long as needed to complete your order and deal with any questions about it.</p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the Data Protection Act, 2019 you have the right to be told how your data is used; to see the data we hold about you; to have it corrected if it is wrong; to have it deleted where we no longer need it; and to object to its use. Contact us to use any of these rights. If you are not satisfied with our answer, you can complain to the Office of the Data Protection Commissioner (<a href="https://www.odpc.go.ke" target="_blank" rel="noopener">odpc.go.ke</a>).</p>

  <h2>8. Keeping it safe</h2>
  <p>This site is served over an encrypted connection, and access to order records is limited to the staff who need them.</p>

  <h2>9. Under 18s</h2>
  <p>This site is for adults only. We do not knowingly collect data from anyone under 18.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes</h2>
  <p>We will update this page if how we use your data changes. The date at the top shows when it last changed.</p>
</LegalPage>
